  {
   "key": "0x106",
   "access": "read",
   "name": "zbus read",
   "aliases": [],
   "regions": [
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:SCC-UserManual-1992.raw.txt",
     "lines": "1151-1169"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80scc.cpp",
     "function": "z80scc_device::zbus_r"
    }
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "In the Z80X30 the registers are addressed by the address on AD7-AD0, latched by the rising edge of /AS.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SCC-UserManual-1992.raw.txt",
       "lines": "1151-1153",
       "sha": "2d40ad69acf57a0a9d96cf056f26a6ae0d813b1e64b0664bcaabb23c40fcab27"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The Shift Right/Shift Left bit in channel B WR0 controls which address bits are decoded to form the register address.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SCC-UserManual-1992.raw.txt",
       "lines": "1153-1157",
       "sha": "7fcb5339338b45aaa930238e0b7b47dd6744234878f9ae9c7697a833d67cb5cd"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "A hardware reset forces Shift Left mode, where the address is decoded from AD5-AD1.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SCC-UserManual-1992.raw.txt",
       "lines": "1158-1159",
       "sha": "f4269b3cb5e01133d7895fb7f62dc9ff148faae55b6f3a6281491673ebb1e533"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "4",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "In Shift Right mode the address is decoded from AD4-AD0, and the Shift bit is written by a command so a WR0 write does not depend on it.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SCC-UserManual-1992.raw.txt",
       "lines": "1159-1162",
       "sha": "2f8fb3dcbf119803ba63938479adaf08147cc0177a7fbcb675c446219c59a19e"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "5",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "In Shift Left mode the register address is on AD4-AD1 and the channel select is AD5; in Shift Right mode the channel select is AD0.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SCC-UserManual-1992.raw.txt",
       "lines": "1163-1169",
       "sha": "d1a2a0c9ffb4a1c2f3374ad8caf079c28ffe28861e1a8fba00cd84922107cdd2"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "6",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "mame",
     "text": "zbus_r takes the shift-left channel from offset bit 4 and the register from bits 3-0, one address line below the document's AD5 and AD4-AD1.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80scc.cpp",
       "lines": "834-836",
       "sha": "6f13ff8deed15142e869037245ebd1b30256c11d0bcafb36d0d14c7c1f4375f9"
      },
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80scc.cpp",
       "lines": "840-843",
       "sha": "161125890a7f983d2d168ec2858fd0a6e5a7924ebe3964609bd55ee66bab7003"
      }
     ],
     "vs": "differs",
     "row": "5"
    }
   ],
